  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved access and provision of lifesaving health, child protection and WASH services in the most vulnerable communities and institutions in the states of Amazonas, Apure, and Sucre.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide Child Protection, Health and WASH assistance to people affected by negative socioeconomic conditions and climate change in Amazoas, Apure and Sucre Regions. This UNICEF project provides improved access to health, child protection and WASH services . The project provides humanitarian assistance to 61,879 people, including 11,264 women, 10,659 men, 39,956 children, and including 1,721 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
